      "message": "I really think this is redundant and asymmetric with what we currently do with the rw and md commands.\n\n1) We should maintain the same access level across rw and md commands.\nhttps://github.com/coreboot/chrome-ec/blob/master/common/memory_commands.c#L113\nhttps://github.com/coreboot/chrome-ec/blob/master/common/memory_commands.c#L197\n\n2) FPMCU is the only board to enable this mechanism, thus it impacts no other boards when CMD_FLAG_RESTRICTED is added to the console declaration. This is verifiable with compare_build.sh too (I think something like ./util/compare_build.sh -b \"+all -fp\"). Furthermore, the future boards that decide to enable this mechanism can choose how they want to restrict these commands using console_is_restricted function as intended (instead of needing to alter this macro logic to and adding console_is_restricted function).\n\nRecommendation:\n--\u003e Remove #ifdef on FP.",
